.TH AS 1 "July 5, 2026" "ReBSD"
.SH NAME
as \- ReBSD MIPS assembler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B as
[
.B \-gkuvxX
]
[
.B \-o
.I outfile
]
[
.B \-I
.I dir
]
[
.B \-EL
|
.B \-EB
]
[
.B \-mips3
|
.B \-march=vr4300
|
.B \-mips32
|
.B \-mips32r2
|
.B \-march=mips32r2
]
[
.I infile
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B as
assembles MIPS source into the ReBSD
.B a.out
object format used by the native toolchain.
The accepted input syntax is the GCC/PCC MIPS assembler syntax emitted by
the ReBSD C compiler driver.
.PP
If
.I infile
is not specified, input is read from standard input.
The output file defaults to
.IR a.out ;
normal compiler invocations pass
.B \-o
explicitly.
.PP
The assembler supports the standard ReBSD text, data, bss, rodata,
constructor, destructor, and exception\-frame sections, MIPS relocation
records, and the
.B .set reorder
and
.B .set noreorder
instruction scheduling modes required by compiler output.
The selected CPU mode controls instruction acceptance and the text alignment
policy used for compiler-generated code.
For legacy
.B a.out
objects, the assembler also preserves the alignment requested by read-only
data sections when writable data and read-only data are packed into the single
output data segment.  This is required by 8-byte MIPS floating-point loads.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " outfile"
Write the object file to
.IR outfile .
.TP
.B \-u
Treat undefined symbols as errors.
.TP
.B \-x
Discard local symbols.
.TP
.B \-X
Discard local symbols whose names start with
.B L
or
.BR . .
.TP
.B \-EL
Emit little\-endian
.B a.out
objects.
.TP
.B \-EB
Emit big\-endian
.B a.out
objects.
.TP
.B \-mips3
.TQ
.B \-march=vr4300
Enable the VR4300\-compatible instruction checks used by the N64 and
Malta64 compatibility ports.
Instructions known to require later MIPS32 revisions are rejected.
Text sections are finished on an 8-byte boundary for this mode so hard-float
VR4300 code can safely load in-text double constants.
.TP
.B \-mips32
.TQ
.BI \-march= mips32
Use the generic MIPS32 acceptance mode.
.TP
.B \-mips32r2
.TQ
.BI \-march= mips32r2
Use the MIPS32 revision 2 acceptance mode used by the Malta port.
This enables MIPS32r2 instructions rejected by the VR4300 mode and uses the
Malta 4-byte text alignment policy.
.TP
.BI \-I " dir"
Accepted for compiler\-driver compatibility.
.TP
.B \-g
.TQ
.B \-k
.TQ
.BI \-O level
Accepted for compiler\-driver compatibility.
.TP
.B \-\-target\-info
Print the assembler target defaults and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/asXXXXXX
Temporary files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cc (1),
.BR pcc (1),
.BR ld (1),
.BR nm (1),
.BR a.out (5)
